        "original_id": "686c5e84-9677-5bb1-8d29-275b9f9070a3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Jerk\n- People: Dennis Cooper, Gisèle Vienne, Jonathan Capdevielle, Dean Corll, David Brooks, Elmer Wayne Henley Jr.\n- Places: Houston, Texas\n- Topics: puppet plays, serial killings\n\nFacts:\n- Dean Arnold Corll was born on December 24, 1939, and died on August 8, 1973.\n- From 1970 to 1973 in Houston, Texas, Dean Corll and his teenaged accomplices David Brooks and Elmer Wayne Henley Jr. abducted, raped, tortured, and murdered at least 28 boys.\n- Dennis Cooper published the novel Jerk in 1993.\n- Jerk is a one-person puppet play by American writer Dennis Cooper.\n- The play Jerk was made in collaboration with director Gisèle Vienne and performer Jonathan Capdevielle.\n- The play Jerk is based on Dennis Cooper's 1993 novel of the same name.",
